# M4.23 stopped preparation partial boundary

- Date: 2026-08-28
- Server: `ubuntu-8gb-nbg1-2` via Tailscale `100.121.130.51`
- Control commit executed: `30b4531449ec05b30afe0097eb69e1cb569590da`
- Command phase: versioned `prepare`; no first-start or unit-install phase

## Failure

The application clone used
`git@github.com:Tausendunde1nz/adult-publishing-core.git`. The `chatops`
server identity received `Repository not found`, so the transaction stopped
before immutable releases, venv, migrations, configuration or state existed.

The EXIT handler then reported `backup_timer_paused: unbound variable`. The
handler referenced a function-local variable after Bash had unwound that
scope. It therefore did not restore the encrypted-backup timer.

## Exact observed partial state

- STAGING-S1 remains active.
- Commercial service/unit, release root, configuration root and state root are
  absent; no migration ran and no first start occurred.
- The commercial-aware backup script is installed at reviewed SHA-256
  `0de61224be517e08fd0a789673df7977f0581aa92608513d99ca9a26ad4bebe8`.
- The locked OS identity exists, is not in `chatops`, and the versioned minimal
  traversal ACL gate passes.
- The exact PostgreSQL peer rule/mapping gate passes. The migrator/runtime
  roles and empty database exist.
- The staging directory exists but has no children.
- Root-private rollback copies of the previous backup script, `pg_hba.conf`
  and `pg_ident.conf` exist under
  `/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/m4-23-commercial-s0-stopped-installation/20260828T15-39-59Z`.
- The encrypted-backup service is inactive and its timer is temporarily
  inactive. The next planned run was more than eleven hours away.

## Authorized recovery plan

1. Resolve the exact repository/credential route read-only from existing
   server Git metadata; do not create another release path.
2. Version and test a recovery mode that accepts only the exact partial state,
   resumes the backup timer safely, and continues without recreating existing
   identities/database/mapping.
3. Make the timer-trap state global so every later error resumes the timer.
4. Merge and synchronize the repair before any server write.
5. Run the recovery preflight, resume the timer, then continue the stopped
   preparation. Abort on any state outside this exact boundary.

No destructive rollback, database drop, identity deletion, ACL removal,
PostgreSQL restoration or path cleanup is authorized by this diagnosis.

## Repository route result

The canonical application remote uses the failing `github.com` host alias,
whose configured private key does not match the public deploy key registered
on the application repository. The working `github.com-infra` alias is scoped
to Control and must not be reused as an application credential. No credential
will be copied, rotated or broadened in M4.23.

The reviewed recovery therefore accepts one root-owned mode-0600 Git bundle at
an exact `/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/m4-23-input/` path. The bundle is created
from a depth-one fetch of the final application main commit, transferred only
over Tailscale SSH, bound by SHA-256 at execution, verified with `git bundle
verify`, and still required to produce the exact application commit/tree and a
clean, complete Git object graph. Control continues through its existing,
working `github.com-infra` read route.
